    "Baseline is the previous KV reservation version; both versions remeasured in ABBA order with complete 48-layer Naive NVFP4 model, 8 GPUs in layer placement, max_batch1/MTP0, BF16 activation/KV, chunk512/context65536, 16 threads and no history/prefix cache.",
    "No concurrent profiling, compilation or GPU polling during native timed requests. All outputs and reasoning, including warmups, agree across versions; each code-generation case passes 980 checks.",
    "The legacy FP16 planar NVFP4 route-capacity failure is reproduced under memcheck at 16 experts, batch9, topk16. Candidate passes the same case plus alternative shapes and CUDA Graph replay.",
    "Aligned KV trim, specialized SWA and 16-head IndexScores fast paths are retained. Unsupported Indexer block widths are rejected explicitly; this does not claim support for arbitrary quantization formats.",
    "Memory snapshots are retained allocator pools after requests, not peak usage. Conservative small-batch route storage adds about 26.25 KiB per 256-expert layer in this configuration.",
    "End-to-end benchmark covers ordinary decoding with MTP disabled. Other GPU architectures were not tested; no broad performance claim outside measured configurations."
